# Chapter 5, part 6: the messages of the markers.

.h2 Messages of the markers [markers-messages]
.ix Marker messages
.ix Messages of the markers
.ix Invalid marker selection
.ix No string specified
.ix Marker type cannot be edited
.ix Not a valid number
.ix Cannot find section number
.ix Counter must be 1 to 99
The messages that the marker commands and panels give, and the texts that
stand in the place of a marker, are listed here with what to do about each.  The
messages of the other commands are in {n:messages}.  A message of the panels is
shown in a small box over the panel with the words Press any key under it; after
a key the panel is as it was.  A message of the Marker command itself is shown
in
the same way or on the message line at the foot of the screen, as the table
says.
.h3 When a marker is chosen
.table 23 11 23
Message | Where | Cause and what to do
Invalid marker selection (Not | Box titled | The Cross-reference marker was
 available in an unstructured | Marker | chosen in an unstructured
 document) |  | document.  It refers to a
  |  | section and an unstructured
  |  | document has none.  Make the
  |  | document structured
  |  | ({n:edit-b-structured}), or
  |  | use another marker.
Invalid marker selection (Not | Box titled | Page Number or Section was chosen
 available in document body) | Marker | in the text of a document.  They
  |  | stand only in a header or a
  |  | footer ({n:format-page-headers}).
Marker type N cannot be | Message line | {k:Alt-F12} was pressed on a
 edited |  | marker that Strata cannot
  |  | change, as a document made
  |  | by another program can
  |  | hold; N is its type number.
  |  | The marker can be deleted,
  |  | not changed.
.end
The name of the Cross-reference marker is in parentheses in the Marker Commands
table of an unstructured document, and the names of Page Number and Section are
in parentheses in every document, so that a marker that the command does not
accept is seen before it is chosen ({n:markers-what}).
.h3 On a marker panel
These are shown over the panel when {k:Ins} is pressed, and no marker is made
until the panel is accepted.
