  |  | no sign, no point).  Type
  |  | a number in that range.
Cannot find section | Cross-reference (Section | There is no section of
 number | Number) | the document with that
  |  | number.  Type a section
  |  | number that the document
  |  | has, such as 1.2, or move
  |  | to the section before
  |  | choosing the marker
  |  | ({n:marker-cross-reference}).
.end
The panels check the fields in the order in which they stand, and give the
message for the first field that is wrong.  A field of the Keycap panel that
shows
a value in brackets, such as [0.0], is not checked; it has no value of its own.
.h3 In the editor of a note, a comment, an equation or a LaTeX marker
.table 32 28
Message | Where
Press Ins to Save Changes or Esc to | The status line of the editor of a
 Restore Previous Version | Note or a Comment.
Ins saves, Esc restores, {k:Ctrl-W} views | The status line of the editor of an
 the equation | Equation.
Press Ins to Save Changes or Esc to | The status line of the editor of a
 Restore Previous Version | LaTeX marker (LATEX EDIT).
.end
{k:Ins} keeps the text and goes on to the panel of the marker; {k:Esc} gives up
the
changes and the whole marker command.
.h3 When a picture cannot be shown on the screen
In the X11 version the picture of a Picture marker is shown in the text.  When
it cannot be shown, the label of the marker is shown instead, and the reason is
one of these texts.
.table 32 28
Message | Cause
The picture has no file name | The File Name field of the marker is
  | empty.
LaTeX cannot read that kind of picture | The name of the file does not end in
 file (use PNG, JPEG, PDF or EPS) | {c:.png}, {c:.jpg}, .jpeg, {c:.pdf} or .eps.
The picture file cannot be read | The file is not there, or it cannot
  | be read by the account that runs the
  | Editor.
LaTeX could not make the picture (is | The file ends in a right name but is
 the file a valid image?) | damaged or is not a picture.
The picture is too large or has no | The picture that was made is wider or
 size | taller than 20000 dots, or has no size.
The picture has too many pixels | The picture that was made has more than
  | eight million dots (for example 4000 by
  | 2000).  Make it smaller: a smaller Width
  | or Height, or a lower Scale.
The picture file is cut off | The picture that was made is not complete.
The picture file or data is | The picture that was made is damaged;
 damaged | the message shows what is wrong (the
  | data, the palette or the colors).
An interlaced picture is not | The picture that was made is stored in
 supported | the interlaced form, which is not shown.
.end
A picture is checked before it is shown.  One that fails a check is treated
like a picture that cannot be made: the label is shown and the message shows
why.
The Printer gives no message for a picture that cannot be made: the marker is
printed as a Box, PIC and the name, and the print goes on ({n:marker-picture}).
.h3 Texts that stand in the place of a marker
These are not messages but text that a marker prints or shows.
.table 24 36
Text | Where and why
[no section] | The text of a Cross-reference whose section
  | is gone, on the screen and in print.  Delete
  | the marker or make a new one for another
  | section.
page of 1.2 | The text of a Cross-reference with the style
  | Page Number on the screen, where the page is
  | not known; the printed page has the number
  | ({n:marker-cross-reference}).
Box with the label of the | In print, for the markers of
 marker | {x:markers-labels}, for a marker that
  | Strata cannot change, and for a picture or an
  | equation that cannot be made
  | ({n:markers-printed}).
[Comment by NAME, TIME: TEXT] | A Comment in a Draft print
  | ({n:marker-comment}).
.end
